# KNOWN-EQUIVALENT SITES, one per line, and each one is a claim a human made.
#
# TSV: file <TAB> line <TAB> rule <TAB> digest — DIGEST is the target's blob
# digest at the revision the claim was made against, first 12 chars, which is
# what makes an entry EXPIRE: edit the file and the digest moves, so the entry
# stops silencing a line that has since changed and the survivor is reported
# again.  `tools/mutate' prints the exact rows to paste under every survivor.
#
# EQUIVALENT IS NOT SURVIVED.  A survivor is a claim about the SUITE; an
# equivalent mutant is a rewrite with no observable difference at all, so it is
# counted apart and left out of the score.  Putting a real hole here hides it.

